    "answer": {
      "short": "Cheryl: 47.6% improvement, compared with Jason’s 36.4%.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Jason’s percentage increase} &= \\frac{75-55}{55}\\times100\\%\\\\&\\approx36.4\\%\\\\\\text{Cheryl’s percentage increase} &= \\frac{62-42}{42}\\times100\\%\\\\&\\approx47.6\\%\\end{aligned}$$\nBoth marks increased by 20 percentage points. Cheryl has the greater relative percentage improvement because the increase is a larger percentage of her original mark.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
